From ada6f217692a15e91614bd97d1f5adc7babbdbbc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?R=C3=A9mi=20Bernon?= <rbernon@codeweavers.com>
Date: Sat, 20 Jun 2026 10:32:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 022/285] winewayland: Make window lock mutex recursive.

Every other driver does it, it will make life easier.

Wine already carries the recursive mutex (d0ae5dd3e16) and
initializes it once before registry population (a5bc758619d).
Keep the initialization comment at that call; do not add a second call.
---
 dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland.c b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland.c
index 0f300b1..9474e81 100644
--- a/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland.c
+++ b/dlls/winewayland.drv/wayland.c
@@ -326,6 +326,7 @@ BOOL wayland_process_init(void)
         return FALSE;
     }
 
+    /* initialize win data mutex */
     wayland_window_init();
 
     /* Populate registry */
-- 
2.55.0

